|rarity = N
|name1 = Lizard Cat
|name2 = Dragon Cat
|name3 = King Dragon Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dragon Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''King Dragon Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Use Lizard Cat in combination with tanky units like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]] or [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]] to steamroll over everything in your path. However, be mindful that this cat is single-target, as he won't work well against multiple tough enemies. In such cases, use [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack]] Cats like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]].

A big stack of Dragon/King Dragon Cats protected by meatshields like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] is almost unstoppable throughout [[Empire of Cats]], as well as being fairly effective in [[Into the Future]]. He is incredibly powerful against other ranged bosses when  protected by cat spam. Stack him together with [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]] and [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]] and you will be able to achieve massive DPS, allowing them to easily tear apart certain notorious stages. Furthermore, because of their decently high range, as long as they are protected well, the stack you create is in little danger throughout [[Empire of Cats]].

==='''True Form'''===
True Form improves health and attack stats, at the cost of a longer recharge time. This means that the Evolved Form can stack and deal DPS more efficiently compared to King Dragon and variants stacks. However, you should keep in mind that Dragon costs as much as King Dragon, so the latter is still preferable unless there is an overabundance of money. If you are '''very''' confident in your lineup and know you can spare a few slots, then it is a good but situational idea to use Research Up [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]], [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] or [[Kimono Champs (Combo)|Kimono Champs]], as they can reduce the recharge time of King Dragon to a somewhat okay level.

As you reach the later parts of the game, specifically UL, this unit and his variants' (except talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]) use declines rapidly as you are likely to acquire reliable specialists who are worth more than him. The range advantage also loses out, as Dragons eventually become vulnerable to enemy surges, waves and long distance attacks. He also loses out to other less disposable general backliners like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] simply because of his subpar stats.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner}}

