==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.4 Update|Version 2.0.4]] reduced King Dragon Cat's base health from 1,400 to 900 and base attack from 500 to 400, and increased base recharge from 570f<sup>19s</sup> to 770f<sup>25.67s</sup>.
*Lizard Cat has the highest range of all Normal Cats.
*King Dragon Cat's design may be a reference to [[wikia:ultra:Gomora|Gomora]] from the Ultraman series, as they both sport spikes on their bellies and horns that extend sideways.
*Prior to [[Version 13.5 Update|Version 13.5]], Lizard Cat was the only Normal Cat to be in an [[:Category:Event Cat Capsule|Event Capsule]], being in [[Summer Break Cats (Event Gacha)|Summer Break Cats]] specifically.
*In several [[Nyanko Daisensou 4Koma & Strategy App|4Koma]] comics, Lizard Cat is shown to be able to shed his tail when in danger.
*In Dragon Cat's spritesheet, two of their sprites have a blue pixel in the bottom left corner, which is visible in their attack and knockback animations.
*Prior to [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]], Lizard Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Lizard Cat
Able to attack enemies from a distance.
Powerful single shot long range attack. </pre>
<pre>Dragon Cat
Found its way here from a fantasy world.
Powerful single shot long range attack. </pre>
<pre>King Dragon Cat
Don't ask how he made it into the Dragon Elite.
Excellent long distance attacks.
Powerful single shot long range attack. </pre>
**Dragon Cat's new description contains an error, as it says they are able to deliver "a unrivaled blow" instead of "'''an''' unrivaled blow".

